From e67d9a6d13a007876c2b87035b04566cb3ea39ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 0cwa <0@none.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 02:58:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Keep ordinary media on view-once sync and explain retention
 settings

AI-assisted compatibility changes to the retention controls adapted from
Angus Turnbull's fork. A linked device's view-once open event deleted the
attachments of whatever message it named once view-once retention was off,
including media of a message that is not view-once. Delete only for view-once
messages. The settings now say that turning an option off does not delete
messages or media already kept, and that kept content may appear in backups
and exports, including on another device after restore.
Source-Commit: e67d9a6d13a007876c2b87035b04566cb3ea39ab

---
